{
  "name": "Error Handling | Main — Error Handler",
  "description": "Started by n8n itself whenever a workflow that names it as its error workflow fails. Classifies the alert P1-P4, alerts in Telegram, Slack and email by priority, and logs to Google Sheets and Notion.",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-title",
      "name": "Title",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -160,
        -304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Error Handling — Main Workflow\n\nSystem-wide error handler for all n8n workflows. Set as the `errorWorkflow` on every other production workflow — n8n invokes this automatically when a linked workflow fails.\n\n**Sections on this canvas:**\n1. **Main / Classify & Notify** — Error Trigger fires → classifies severity (P1–P4) → sends Telegram + Slack/Gmail alerts by priority.\n2. **Logger** (runs inline, right after Main, for every priority P1–P4) — appends the error to Google Sheets and creates a Notion page.\n3. **Owner Notifier** (runs inline, right after Main, for P1–P3 only — P4 is too low-severity to page an owner) — looks up which owner tag is on the failed workflow and DMs them on Slack if it's not the primary owner.\n\nThe separate **Watchdog** workflow (its own Schedule Trigger, own deployment) lives alongside this one under the same `error-handling/` project folder, but is NOT merged here — it runs independently every 4 hours, not as a step in this execution.",
        "height": 196,
        "width": 2804,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-main",
      "name": "Main Section Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -160,
        -32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Main — Classify & Notify\n\nTriggered by: Error Trigger, fired automatically by n8n when a linked workflow fails (this workflow set as that workflow's `errorWorkflow`)\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Receives the error payload from the failed workflow\n2. Normalizes it and classifies a priority: P1 (critical/payment/OOM), P2 (auth/sync/4xx), P3 (5xx/timeout), P4 (everything else)\n3. Routes by priority to the matching Telegram + Slack (P1–P3) or Telegram + Gmail (P4) alert\n4. Flows inline into the Logger section (all priorities) and the Owner Notifier section (P1–P3 only)",
        "height": 880,
        "width": 2758,
        "color": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-logger",
      "name": "Logger Section Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -144,
        912
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Logger\n\nTriggered by: runs inline after Main — Classify & Notify (every priority, P1–P4)\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Appends the error record to Google Sheets\n2. Creates a tracking page in Notion (status: Open)",
        "height": 468,
        "width": 980,
        "color": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-owner",
      "name": "Owner Notifier Section Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        912,
        912
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Owner Notifier\n\nTriggered by: runs inline after Main — Classify & Notify (P1–P3 only — P4 skips this section)\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Looks up the failed workflow's tags via the n8n API\n2. Extracts an `owner:` tag, if any\n3. If the owner isn't the primary owner, looks up their Slack ID\n4. DMs that owner directly on Slack",
        "height": 484,
        "width": 1692,
        "color": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "wf1-trigger",
      "name": "On Workflow Error",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        256
      ],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "wf1-normalize",
      "name": "Normalize & Classify",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        192,
        256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const raw = $input.first().json;\nconst workflowName = raw.workflow?.name || raw.execution?.workflowName || 'unknown';\nconst err = raw.execution?.error || raw.error || {};\nconst errorMsg = (err.message || '').toLowerCase();\nconst failedNode = err.node?.name || raw.execution?.lastNodeExecuted || 'unknown';\nconst workflowId = raw.workflow?.id || raw.execution?.workflowId || '';\nconst executionId = raw.execution?.id || '';\n// n8n builds this link from the server's own address, so local and production alerts each point to the right place\nconst executionUrl = raw.execution?.url || '';\nconst timestamp = new Date().toISOString();\nconst statusMatch = errorMsg.match(/status code (\\d{3})/);\nconst statusCode = statusMatch ? parseInt(statusMatch[1]) : (parseInt(err.httpCode) || 0);\nconst fnLower = failedNode.toLowerCase();\n\nlet priority;\n\nconst overrideMatch = failedNode.match(/\\bp[1-4]\\b/i) || errorMsg.match(/\\bp[1-4]\\b/i);\nif (overrideMatch) {\n  priority = overrideMatch[0].toUpperCase();\n}\nelse if (/payment|stripe|charge|invoice|billing/.test(fnLower) || /payment|stripe|charge|invoice|billing/.test(errorMsg)) {\n  priority = 'P1';\n}\nelse if (/out of memory|oom|killed|sigkill/.test(errorMsg)) {\n  priority = 'P1';\n}\nelse if (statusCode === 401 || statusCode === 403 || /unauthorized|forbidden/.test(errorMsg)) {\n  priority = 'P2';\n}\nelse if (/sync|crm|import|export/.test(fnLower) || /sync|crm|import|export/.test(errorMsg)) {\n  priority = 'P2';\n}\nelse if (statusCode >= 400 && statusCode < 500) {\n  priority = 'P2';\n}\nelse if (statusCode >= 500 || /econnreset|etimedout|timeout/.test(errorMsg)) {\n  priority = 'P3';\n}\nelse {\n  priority = 'P4';\n}\n\n// Agents: anything that stops an agent from working (a tool or the MCP unreachable, a table write failing, the model failing) is at least P2.\n// An output-format / parse error is a new bug that needs a fix now: P1. An explicit P1-P4 tag in the node name always wins.\nconst nodeType = String((err.node && err.node.type) || '').toLowerCase();\nconst agentRelated = /langchain|tool$/.test(nodeType) || /agent|coach|router/i.test(workflowName);\nconst formatError = /output format|output parser|parse|parsing|doesn't fit|does not fit|invalid json|not valid json|unexpected token|malformed/.test(errorMsg);\nif (!overrideMatch && agentRelated) {\n  if (formatError) priority = 'P1';\n  else if (priority === 'P3' || priority === 'P4') priority = 'P2';\n}\n\nreturn [{ json: { priority, workflowName, workflowId, executionId, executionUrl, failedNode, errorMessage: err.message || '', statusCode, timestamp } }];"
      }
    },
